---
// apps/site/src/components/home/Why.astro
//
// The origin story, in the first person. It is the one place on the site that
// may talk about a team moving ahead of its backend, because it is laqi's own
// history rather than a claim about what a reader's team will get: laqi has
// no customers to measure and no study to cite. "was born on" is doing real
// work in that sentence — do not rewrite it into a promise.
---

<section class="why" id="why">
  <div class="left">
    <p class="eyebrow">why it works</p>
    <h2>The team was ready.<br /><em>The endpoints were not.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="right">
    <p>
      laqi was born on a frontend team running two to three sprints ahead of
      its backend. The work was not blocked on design or on decisions — it was
      blocked on endpoints that did not exist yet, one at a time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The fix was not to guess. Both sides wrote down what the API would look
      like, and the frontend built against that agreement instead of against a
      server. When the real endpoints arrived they answered the shape everyone
      had already been working from.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is the whole idea, and the reason laqi keeps the contract as plain
      JSON in your repository rather than in a dashboard somewhere: the thing
      both teams agreed on should be reviewable in a pull request.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 4rem;
    max-width: 82rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 40%, transparent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 68rem) {
    .why {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim2);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  h2 em {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--viol);
  }

  .right p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .right p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
